# Colours for wall.obj.
#
# Every channel is a multiple of 0x11, because the panel is four bits per
# channel and a colour that is not shifts on the device and nowhere else.
# Each Kd is a sixteenth, so obj2cpp's round(v * 255) lands back exactly
# on the byte it was written for.
#
# The top is the lit face and the front is the one the player reads the room
# from, so the front is the mid tone and the sides fall away.

newmtl wall_top
Kd 0.800000 0.733333 0.666667   # #CCBBAA

newmtl wall_face
Kd 0.600000 0.533333 0.466667   # #998877

newmtl wall_side
Kd 0.466667 0.400000 0.333333   # #776655
